From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mikhail Malyshev <mike.malyshev@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 16:10:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/10] ui/dbus: let QEMU_DBUS_REFRESH_MS set the GL listener's
 refresh interval

A GL D-Bus listener showing a 2D console (a virtio-gpu-pci head next to a
virtio-vga-gl one) does not forward that console's damage as it arrives:
dbus_gl_gfx_update() accumulates it and dbus_gl_refresh() sends it on the
GUI refresh timer, GUI_REFRESH_INTERVAL_DEFAULT (30 ms), which the D-Bus
display never changes. The 2D head is capped at about 33 frames/s.

Measured with a 1080p60 clip in a Windows guest: the guest flushed 42-43
frames/s and the console received 30-32. With QEMU_DBUS_REFRESH_MS=16 the
two match.

An environment variable is a stopgap. Upstream, this wants to be a
-display dbus option, or better, the 2D damage sent from a bottom half as
it arrives.

Signed-off-by: Mikhail Malyshev <mike.malyshev@gmail.com>
---
 ui/dbus-listener.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/ui/dbus-listener.c b/ui/dbus-listener.c
index dc7ad0992..f23b9abc3 100644
--- a/ui/dbus-listener.c
+++ b/ui/dbus-listener.c
@@ -1290,5 +1290,17 @@ dbus_display_listener_new(const char *bus_name,
 #endif
     qemu_console_register_listener(con, &ddl->dcl, ops);
 
+    /*
+     * A 2D console's damage reaches the listener only on the refresh timer,
+     * and its default (GUI_REFRESH_INTERVAL_DEFAULT, 30 ms) caps that console
+     * at 33 Hz however fast the guest draws. QEMU_DBUS_REFRESH_MS overrides it.
+     */
+    {
+        const char *r = g_getenv("QEMU_DBUS_REFRESH_MS");
+        if (r && atoi(r) > 0) {
+            qemu_console_listener_set_refresh(&ddl->dcl, atoi(r));
+        }
+    }
+
     return ddl;
 }
